{"created": "2026-10-10T20:16:25.860300+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-10T20:16:26.243069+00:00", "id": 23287623, "conceptrecid": "19574117", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23287623", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.19574117", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23287623", "metadata": {"title": "Ento-Linguistics: Language, Ambiguity, and Scientific Communication in Entomology", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23287623", "publication_date": "2026-10-10", "description": "Ento-Linguistics v1.3.1 is a corpus-custody patch to the v1.3.0 complexity edition. A second exact-text PubMed reconciliation links 59 more archived abstracts to their source records (7,599 of 7,609 now identified; the 10 unreconciled strings stay excluded from headline results), and PMC records titled as corrections, errata, retraction notices or retracted items are excluded from full-text analysis (6,997 of 7,073 stored records analyzed). All analysis layers, both fixed-margin protocols and the vocabulary/threshold diagnostic were regenerated; the paper reports every value from those exports. Six overlapping terminology domains and four source layers retain their descriptive scope; fixed-margin comparisons and heuristic entropy/CACE measures remain distinct from biological interactions, validated meaning or causal reader effects. The 20-minute lecture remains the v1.3.0 GitHub release asset matched to the v1.3.0 paper. Paper figures are CC BY 4.0; software is MIT; source corpus materials retain their providers' terms. Previous version DOIs preserve earlier artifact identities.", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Friedman, Daniel Ari", "affiliation": "Active Inference Institute, APOIDEAS", "orcid": "0000-0001-6232-9096"}, {"name": "Chambers, Tucker Cahill", "affiliation": "APOIDEAS", "orcid": "0009-0008-3793-7872"}], "keywords": ["entomology", "scientific terminology", "language analysis", "discourse analysis", "ant biology", "eusociality", "conceptual frameworks", "active inference", "terminology net